WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.480 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  three years ago I went on my first date  with Brian we had matched on a dating  app and started texting right away he  was so enthusiastic and compassionate he  would text me hey with an exclamation  point followed by how's it going we  really hit it off he was just so easy to  talk to  fast forward to our first date it was  awful  we couldn't keep a conversation going  his voice was monotone he failed to make  eye contact and he wasn't even asking  questions so much for enthusiastic and  compassionate frustrations set in as I  counted down the minutes until freedom  this situation is a prime example of  what I call fictionalizing reality my  conversations with Brian were real but  they were just text on a screen  no body language no vocal cues I was  working with an incomplete picture so to  compensate I colored in what was missing  with bright shades of exuberance and  charm  I had fictionalized my reality  technology had brought me to Brian but  it also introduced ambiguity which  ultimately led to my disappointment we  are more digitally connected than ever  before exchanging on average 250 text  messages and emails every day but only  so much can be said with a digital  message which leads to a number of  challenges in his research on human  communication professor Albert Mehrabian  hints toward some of these challenges  and why technology may interfere with  three critical elements of our  conversation our clarity our intention  and our vulnerability he explains that  our nonverbal cues specifically our tone  of voice and body language help change  the attitudes and feelings of others  more so than the actual words we say let  me give you an example I could say I  can't wait  or I can't wait my tone of voice and  body language help to communicate my  excitement and enthusiasm or lack  thereof he further explains that 93% of  our impact is attributable to these  nonverbal cues where's our actual  content contributes to just 7% this  concept also applies to text messaging  and email our message communicates 7% of  our message but leaving us in the 93  percent darkness where it's hard to  detect clarity intention and  vulnerability as recipients we are often  left feeling confused or doubtful as  senders anxious and misunderstood both  sides are left feeling disconnected but  why first technology compromises clarity  last week I had to cancel plans with my  friend I sent him a quick text  explaining the situation expecting  disappointment a few hours later my  phone buzzed his response it's okay , I  understand  period it's okay I understand  he was definitely mad it's okay I  understand  Oh totally fine but which was it he  hadn't used an emoji or an exclamation  point he must be mad  this conversation had me doubting the  status of our friendship I was  embarrassed by my flakiness I was afraid  to reach out it was unclear what he was  saying I decided I maybe overthinking  everything  so I decided to give him a call sure  enough he did understand and we  rescheduled our dinner for another night  I had fictionalized the 93% of his  message he had only given me 7% and  unfortunately for us as psychology  research shows when we're given  ambiguity we tend to assume the worst  I'm sure as you have experienced even  the smallest language or punctuation  choice can lead to hours days or even  weeks of frustration and resentment  secondly technology compromises  intention prior to starting my MBA  program at Stanford I was a young  business professional on Wall Street  making powerpoints and consuming  caffeine like my job depended on it to  be clear my job did depend on it I had  worked tirelessly on an extensive pitch  deck I was on version 16 when I sent the  document to my boss for a final review  the next morning and email sat at the  top of my Inbox  I took a deep breath and clicked into  the email Thanks  period what are you kidding me did I  make a mistake does he know how long I  spent working on this project there is  no way I'm spending this much time on  the next one n Oh W a Y period this  email from my boss left me feeling  unappreciated and unsupported this this  interaction wasn't uncommon with him but  this last message left me feeling  completely demoralized to the point that  I considered looking for a new role that  is until I ran into my boss and he  congratulated me on a job well done  wait what to my surprise he had been so  incredibly impressed with the pitch deck  that he printed the deck as is replied  with a quick thx and moved on failing to  see the intention behind his thanks I  had fictionalized my reality yet again  when it comes to email and text we are  often overconfident in our ability to  convey our complete thoughts and  feelings assuming that the recipient  shares the same context that we do this  can lead to problems  reducing self-confidence and morale over  time which can deteriorate your  important relationships  lastly technology compromises  vulnerability my phone buzzed as I  received one text message just two words  my body fell within my seat  my dad had informed me that my only  grandfather had passed away but his  message felt abrupt harsh emotionless  what I saw in this moment was support  and strength from my dad but instead I  felt disconnected I was afraid to delve  into the 93% darkness  I couldn't fictionalize this reality  I fail to detect my father's true  feelings and I struggled to expose my  own vulnerability to him again I have  been provided a snippet of content but  the rest was ambiguous it's hard to  choose the right words for a text or  email making it hard to express our true  feelings in important moments like this  one technology allows us to accomplish  incredible things but by virtue of its  digital form it can get in the way of  truth and genuine connection so if you  seek to build meaningful connection how  exactly do you do that strive for  clarity instead of it's okay I  understand try it's okay thanks for  letting me know I'd love to catch up  let's reschedule a clear tone goes a  long way  express your intention explicitly  instead of replying with thanks you  could try this is great I appreciate  your hard work Thanks  with just eight additional words my boss  could have adequately expressed his  appreciation giving me confidence in my  work convey more emotion even when  difficult your grandfather has passed  away I know this is hard for all of us  but stay strong call me when you can I  love you Digital messaging is a powerful  tool and if you use it with intention  you can wield powerful results you can  prevent others from fictionalizing their  reality instead of creating unnecessary  frustration or distance you can build  self-confidence and morale join me in  tackling the dark side of digital  communication so we can build better  relationships  [Applause]  [Music]

